Hohokam is a challenging game to  describe it's full of charm full of  whimsy and is more interested in being  an engaging cognitive experience over a  fast-paced Xterra T challenge in many  ways it reminds me of 2009 s flower  flower at its most basic was a game  about flying around a beautiful world  and activating things however for those  who actually played flower you know it  was so much more than that  Hohokam gave me much the same vibe both  in its play style and presentation in  Hohokam you control what is colloquially  known as the long mover a  rainbow-colored snake-like creature  which flies around the world spreading  music and joy wherever it goes its  journey spans 16 wildly different worlds  each with its own theme and set of  objectives these objectives are yours to  discover though if you pause the game a  little dude will pop up and tell you how  much progress you've made in a  particular world the long mover may need  to do battle against an angry elephant  alongside of fruit throwing monkey or do  something as simple as switching on the  lights  each world is a little different in this  regard and so for my personal favorite  has been the one you're seeing now your  overarching goal here is to shepherd all  these little people around to where they  want to go some want to ride the seesaw  some want to admire themselves in the  funhouse mirror while others still want  to hop on the roller coaster the  expressive blend of color and music on  display here is a perfect example of  Hohokam at its best it's joyous and  upbeat and a delight to explore and  explore you shall as there is no death  and ko hokum nor can you really fail in  your mission  in fact many objectives can be completed  simply by playing around in the world  and watching what happens as I said  earlier the game is more interested in  engaging your senses instead of just  your thumbs if you get hung up on a  particular task or a simply tire of the  current world you can easily hop to  another and find some  completely different all this  exploration is a solo effort however as  Hohokam has no cooperative or  multiplayer aspects to speak up if that  floats your boat you can pick up the  game on August 12th for PlayStation 3  PlayStation 4 and PlayStation Vita  the game features cross by meaning when  you buy one bridge in the game you get  the other two free as well as cross save  meaning you can quit your game and pick  up where ever you left off on any of  those three devices thanks for watching  and I'll see you next time
 

